        "ai_gen_block_40673d6_9QyCfC": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_40673d6",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
            "heading_size": 36,
            "heading_weight": "300",
            "heading_color": "#224b0c",
            "subtitle": "Everything you need to know about our lab-grown diamonds",
            "subtitle_size": 16,
            "subtitle_color": "#053931",
            "subtitle_spacing": 16,
            "header_spacing": 50,
            "faq_1_question": "What are lab-grown diamonds?",
            "faq_1_answer": "<p>Lab-grown diamonds are real diamonds created in controlled laboratory environments using advanced technology that replicates the natural diamond formation process. They have the same physical, chemical, and optical properties as mined diamonds.</p>",
            "faq_2_question": "How to buy lab-grown diamonds?",
            "faq_2_answer": "<p>Browse our collection of certified lab-grown diamonds, select your preferred cut, carat, color, and clarity. Add to cart and complete your purchase securely. Each diamond comes with a certification of authenticity and detailed specifications.</p>",
            "faq_3_question": "Are lab-grown diamonds real?",
            "faq_3_answer": "<p>Yes, lab-grown diamonds are 100% real diamonds. They are chemically, physically, and optically identical to mined diamonds. The only difference is their origin - one is created in a lab, the other formed naturally underground over billions of years.</p>",
            "faq_4_question": "What is the difference between natural and lab-grown diamonds?",
            "faq_4_answer": "<p>The primary difference is origin. Natural diamonds form deep within the Earth over billions of years, while lab-grown diamonds are created in weeks using advanced technology. Both are real diamonds with identical properties, but lab-grown diamonds are more sustainable and typically cost 30-40% less.</p>",
            "faq_5_question": "Do lab-grown diamonds come with certification?",
            "faq_5_answer": "<p>Yes, all our lab-grown diamonds come with certification from internationally recognized gemological laboratories such as IGI, GIA, or GCAL. Each certificate details the diamond's cut, color, clarity, carat weight, and confirms its lab-grown origin.</p>",
            "faq_6_question": "How are lab-grown diamonds made?",
            "faq_6_answer": "<p>Two main methods: <strong>HPHT</strong> (High Pressure High Temperature), which mimics the heat and pressure conditions deep in the earth, and <strong>CVD</strong> (Chemical Vapor Deposition), which grows a diamond layer by layer from carbon-rich gas. Both start from a small diamond \"seed.\"</p>",
            "faq_7_question": "Can you tell a lab-grown diamond from a natural one by looking at it?",
            "faq_7_answer": "<p>No — not with the naked eye, and typically not even under a standard jeweler's loupe. Distinguishing them requires specialized equipment (like a diamond-type tester) that detects trace growth patterns or inclusions unique to each origin.</p>",
